  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Stýrivolt. Logic: rules.objective and rules.gameplay; Karnöffel-style ranking and chalk-up scoring.',
    Player: 'Stýrivolt: four players in partnerships, 48-card deck (tens removed), 9 cards each, 12-card stock. Two chosen suits per deal; no follow suit. Win 5 of 9 tricks; vol (first 5) scores bonus.',
    objective: "Each partnership aims to win at least five of the nine tricks. The team that wins the majority scores on a chalk-up by erasing strokes; the first side to erase all three strokes (or eliminate the opponents' crosses) scores a cross. Making vol (winning the first five tricks) or taking all nine tricks scores extra.",
    gameplay: "The player to the left of the dealer leads to the first trick. Play is clockwise. Any card may be played; there is no requirement to follow suit or to beat the lead. Trick winner is determined by the game's ranking: permanent stikkar and chosen-suit stikkar beat other cards; chosen sevens (lambs) win the trick when led but cannot lead to the first trick. Whoever wins a trick leads to the next. A team that has taken five tricks may stop or continue; taking the first five (vol) or all nine scores bonus strokes.",
    keyRules: [
      'No requirement to follow suit.',
      'Two chosen suits per deal, determined by dealer from stock.',
      'Permanent and chosen-suit stikkar outrank normal cards; lambs (chosen 7s) win when led.',
      'Trader (chosen 5) may be exchanged for the exposed card of that suit.',
      'Hand with no stikkar may exchange hand for the stock before the first trick is complete.',
    ],
